# Competency (executable lift): "What proof dependency DAG underlies this theorem, and how
# does its proof decompose into sub-goals and steps?" — asked of the OUTPUT OF THE REAL
# LIFTER, not of a hand-authored example graph.
#
# The producer-namespace twin of proof-dependency-graph-and-subgoals.rq. That query
# interrogates the prose-authored tests/fixtures/bridges.ttl scene; this one interrogates
# tests/fixtures/lifted-proof.ttl — the byte-exact output of
# gmeow_math::producers::proof_lift, which parses the committed TSTP derivation
# crates/math-lift/fixtures/theorem-subclass.tstp. This is the one bridge whose law spine
# claims a section/retraction rung, so it is also the sharpest evidence: every step name,
# inference rule, and parent edge here came out of a parser, and the DAG's shape is a fact
# about the derivation rather than an authored illustration.
#
# One row per proof step: the run produces a math:ProofDependencyGraph and a math:Proof,
# and the proof decomposes into a logic:GoalExpression sub-goal (math:provesGoal) and its
# math:ProofStep members.
PREFIX math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?run ?dag ?proof ?goal ?step WHERE {
    ?run a math:ProofIngestRun .
    ?dag gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ?run ;
         a math:ProofDependencyGraph .
    ?proof gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ?run ;
           a math:Proof ;
           math:provesGoal ?goal ;
           math:proofStep ?step .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?run), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/producers/"))
}
ORDER BY ?run ?goal ?step
